[b]Filename cleanup / normalization[/b]
The search term is cleaned up automatically by:
[list]
[*]replacing ., _, and - with spaces
[*]replacing ae, oe, ue with ä, ö, ü
[*]removing season / episode markers like S01, S01E02, or Season 1
[*]trimming everything after the first detected year
[/list]


[b]Installation[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Install the [b]Tampermonkey[/b] browser extension
[*]Open [b][url=https://anonym.es/?<RAW_SCRIPT>]ArrActivityQueueSearch.user.js[/url][/b]
[*]Tampermonkey should open the install page automatically
[*]Confirm the installation
[/list]
If you prefer, you can also create a new userscript manually in the Tampermonkey dashboard, paste the code, and save it.


[b]Configuration[/b]
The script comes with safe default @match entries for localhost and the default Radarr/Sonarr ports.
If your instances use different IPs, hostnames, or ports, add your own matches in Tampermonkey:
[list]
[*]Open [b]Tampermonkey Dashboard[/b]
[*]Go to [b]Installed Userscripts[/b]
[*]Edit the script
[*]Open the script’s [b]Settings[/b] tab
[*]Add your custom [b]Includes/Excludes[/b] → [b]User matches[/b]
[/list]
Examples:
[code]
192.168.178.50:7878/activity/queue
http://192.168.178.50:8989/activity/queue
radarr.local:7878/activity/queue
http://sonarr.local:8989/activity/queue
[/code]
You can also add extra @match lines manually in the script header, but keep in mind those may be overwritten when the script gets updated.


